@startuml
title MicroLA C++ Standard Feature Progression

skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "C++11 (Baseline - Required)" <<Rectangle>> #FFE6E6 {
    component "Core Language" as cpp11core
    note right of cpp11core
        • constexpr functions (single return)
        • static_assert
        • alignas(16) for SIMD
        • noexcept
        • nullptr
        • auto type deduction
        • Range-based for loops
        • std::initializer_list
        • Variadic templates

        **MicroLA Support:**
        100% functional, all features
        available on C++11 compilers
    end note
}

package "C++14 Enhancements" <<Rectangle>> #E6F3FF {
    component "MICROLA_CONSTEXPR14" as cpp14
    note right of cpp14
        • Relaxed constexpr:
          - Multiple statements
          - Loops in constexpr
          - Local variables

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        identity() with loops
        Generic matrix operations
        Runtime/compile-time dual use
    end note
}

package "C++17 Features" <<Rectangle>> #E6FFE6 {
    component "MICROLA_IF_CONSTEXPR" as cpp17
    note right of cpp17
        • if constexpr (compile-time branches)
        • inline variables
        • structured bindings

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        SIMD path selection
        Optimized code generation
        Zero runtime overhead
    end note
}

package "C++20 Features" <<Rectangle>> #FFF0E6 {
    component "Modern Features" as cpp20
    note right of cpp20
        • Concepts:
          - Arithmetic<T>
          - FloatingPoint<T>
          - Integral<T>
        • MICROLA_BIT_CAST (std::bit_cast)
        • consteval, constinit

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        Type-safe templates
        Branch optimization
        Safe type punning
        Compile-time validation
    end note
}

package "C++23 Enhancements" <<Rectangle>> #FFE6F3 {
    component "MICROLA_IF_CONSTEVAL" as cpp23
    note right of cpp23
        • if consteval
        • Deducing this

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        Dual compile/runtime paths
        Optimized constexpr detection
    end note
}

package "C++26 (Latest)" <<Rectangle>> #F0E6FF {
    component "MICROLA_CONSTEXPR_TRIG" as cpp26
    note right of cpp26
        • constexpr math functions:
          - std::sin, std::cos
          - std::sqrt, std::atan2

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        Compile-time rotations
        Arbitrary angle matrices
        Full constexpr transformation

        **Example:**
        constexpr auto rot =
          Mat<float,2,2>::rotation(45°);
    end note
}

cpp11core -down-> cpp14 : Adds
cpp14 -down-> cpp17 : Adds
cpp17 -down-> cpp20 : Adds
cpp20 -down-> cpp23 : Adds
cpp23 -down-> cpp26 : Adds

note as FeatureDetection
    **Automatic Feature Detection:**

    #if __cplusplus >= 201402L
      #define MICROLA_CONSTEXPR14 constexpr
    #else
      #define MICROLA_CONSTEXPR14 inline
    #endif

    Features automatically enabled
    based on compiler __cplusplus value
end note

@enduml
